div.div:
chrȳsŏprăsus ,
			i, m., = χρυσόπρασος, 
I.the chrysoprase, a precious
				stone of a golden-yellow and a leek-green color, Plin.  37, 5, 20, § 77;
				Prud. Psych. 865;
					Isid. Orig. 16, 7, 7;
				16, 14, 8; Ambros. in Psa.
				118, Serm. 16, § 41 sq.; also called chrȳsŏ-prăsĭus
				lăpis , Plin. 37,
				8, 34, § 113.
